{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
Oh, [Em]Polly, pretty Polly, come [D]go along with [Em]me,
[Em]Polly, pretty Polly, come [D]go along with [Em]me,
Be[Em]fore we get [D]married some [Em]pleasure to see.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
He [Em]led her over mountains and [D]valleys so [Em]deep,
He [Em]led her over mountains and [D]valleys so [Em]deep,
Pretty [Em]Polly mis[D]trusted and [Em]then began to weep.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 3"}
Oh, [Em]Willie, oh, Willie, I'm a[D]fraid of your [Em]ways,
Oh, [Em]Willie, oh, Willie, I'm a[D]fraid of your [Em]ways,
I'm a[Em]fraid you will [D]lead my poor [Em]body astray.
{end_of_verse}
{x_end: Em}
